4. Configuration Workflow Sequence Diagram (config_sequence.puml)
Shows how the user updates the system behavior via the Web UI.

@startuml config_sequence
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant "Browser" as UI
participant "Flask Server" as Flask
participant "Global Configuration" as Config

== View Settings ==
User -> UI: Click "Settings"
UI -> Flask: GET /settings
Flask -> Config: Read current values
Config --> Flask: Return {hardware, logging, timing}
Flask --> UI: Render HTML Form

== Apply Changes ==
User -> UI: Change Freq to 10Hz
User -> UI: Toggle CSV Off
User -> UI: Click "Save"
UI -> Flask: POST /settings (freq=10, csv=false)

Flask -> Flask: Calculate Interval (1 / 10 = 0.1s)
Flask -> Config: Update config_timing["SAMPLING_INTERVAL"]
Flask -> Config: Update config_logging["ENABLE_CSV_LOGGING"]

Flask -> UI: Flash "Settings Saved"
Flask -> UI: Redirect /dashboard

== Runtime Effect ==
note right of Config
  DAQ Engine (running in background)
  will pick up these changes 
  on the next loop iteration.
end note

@enduml